<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Business</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Business</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-bus</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-bus" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1431?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-bus" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nvidia reinstates former CEO Jensen Huang despite China espionage scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5de9af46a1a1fe0895206f3156ffed3855c922adf2af53c68a52d8ccac81212</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926--88659c21678b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's board voted unanimously to bring back the disgraced CEO, who resigned this month amid news of his affairs. He's suspected of having had a relationship with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'I've lost her forever' — Why German voice actors are refusing to sign Netflix's AI contract</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8b29e578311ba4d9399667e9c683913b6e2f79058d3eef0d95778549d1429cc</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381--da3277b6e37b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For decades, Germans have known Hollywood's biggest stars through the same familiar voices. Now an AI clause in Netflix contracts is splitting the industry over whether it protects performers or exposes them.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Early Start Pension: Can child investment accounts help?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f4397cfc6ff26114d77407f018346d6624c838e752808f4071305ffb6d21baf</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-early-start-pension-can-child-investment-accounts-help/a-79852185--25ffc2424261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-early-start-pension-can-child-investment-accounts-help/a-79852185?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany plans to pay €10 a month into investment accounts for children to encourage long-term retirement saving. Economists say the measure may help build wealth but won't solve the country's pension funding challenge.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Can German auto manufacturing recover after Mercedes and VW cuts?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01a42890943eade1a72eb2d64a72e6609cabca4810252ca9f0f5c503d7d237b8</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-german-auto-manufacturing-recover-after-mercedes-and-vw-cuts/a-79946928--88277c189f1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-german-auto-manufacturing-recover-after-mercedes-and-vw-cuts/a-79946928?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German automakers are pulling back on investments at home, sparking fresh anxiety about the auto sector's future. Some industry watchers think there is still a narrow window to stem the decline. But how?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Lufthansa to cut 1,000 jobs, citing ongoing losses — reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:701e1877b412f0d07cb847452f036915754cb21300b232230c17166a6caa9e84</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062--a7b4260396ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lufthansa-to-cut-1-000-jobs-citing-ongoing-losses-reports/a-80000062?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to a letter obtained by the media, Lufthansa's executive board said the German company is losing €20 million every month. In addition to job cuts, operational cuts are also planned.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Anthropic trading tests investors' appetite for AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8305ddc9c833179645480c5495ec4c48a09445c3391c4a6fd4050f52b245a881</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/anthropic-trading-tests-investors-appetite-for-ai/a-79993163--d18c2700770b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/anthropic-trading-tests-investors-appetite-for-ai/a-79993163?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anthropic was valued at $2 trillion after shares started trading on the Nasdaq following a record $81 billion IPO. Its performance will put investor confidence in AI to the test.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Iran balances ties with China and Russia as Trump ramps up pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d3fa94583c62ff14299e7fef535be0205f48cdff80e6097a053a4be7f2e9ad7</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-balances-ties-with-china-and-russia-as-trump-ramps-up-pressure/a-79979920--3c92417b16df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-balances-ties-with-china-and-russia-as-trump-ramps-up-pressure/a-79979920?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Donald Trump seeks to tighten economic pressure on Iran, China remains its biggest oil customer and Russia a key partner. But both powers are balancing support for Tehran against broader interests with Washington.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Is the AI bubble bursting just as Anthropic goes public?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dd75e4a463463c1d9151b335884222ca10a8ebf6c66c4cb5e6d14764420dbea</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537--10f78cdc2264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sharp sell-off in tech stocks after the US midterms and the Nvidia scandal has cast doubt on Anthropic's IPO. Yet with hundreds of billions still being invested, some think the AI party is still in full swing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia forms national security committee after Huang affair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac9e9db9edbca8ae0350b9b8675a823ffce8440aa0c1478674509b861f63c12f</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-forms-national-security-committee-after-huang-affair/a-79970447--7d1c93df3ff0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-forms-national-security-committee-after-huang-affair/a-79970447?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia has created a board-level committee for national security and export control. This follows the resignation of CEO Jensen Huang over extramarital affairs, allegedly including one with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Could the Airbus €3 billion loan row reignite a US-EU trade dispute?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e96c20e4708b64ef744a6dfe5775ad4f061a3f33a42ceb60a4970ef01fa8f04e</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-the-airbus-_3-billion-loan-row-reignite-a-us-eu-trade-dispute/a-79943075--30f362f3b820.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-the-airbus-€3-billion-loan-row-reignite-a-us-eu-trade-dispute/a-79943075?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US says a record €3 billion financing package for Airbus may conflict with a transatlantic aircraft-subsidy truce. EU officials insist the funding complies with market-based rules.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Jensen Huang: Spy row, affairs leave Nvidia without its rockstar CEO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c2a689b6ad7506cd63c4be432ec0ad5fbd00e7b6e9c3cd7e25daad7e5d7d927</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972--e6a7da621d57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jensen-huang-spy-row-affairs-leave-nvidia-without-its-rockstar-ceo/a-79926972?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang, who built Nvidia into the world’s dominant AI chipmaker, is stepping down as CEO over extramarital affairs. DW examines how losing its figurehead will affect the firm and the US-China AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f92f4554ac703dae27150bf2bc3b4cc22ac4d8f2f25dd66fba3c71a17d59abeb</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Megaspeed and the battle to go high-end Nvidia chips into China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d538106e1eba50806ef72fd6b99c0cbc2d33dc7450569884208dc253525fffc8</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129--5e400fbb45fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/megaspeed-and-the-battle-to-go-high-end-nvidia-chips-into-china/a-79909129?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jensen Huang's affair with a suspected Chinese spy has shone a light on Megaspeed, the company she worked for. It is under investigation in the US for smuggling Nvidia chips into China, which it denies.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why Nvidia CEO's affair with alleged Chinese spy matters for AI race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2eefd5cff86fd9d9f87c8bc56530d6ee9eace603113f236383a4bf9f7375653b</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-nvidia-ceo-s-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy-matters-for-ai-race/a-79898338--07d9155781b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-nvidia-ceo-s-affair-with-alleged-chinese-spy-matters-for-ai-race/a-79898338?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang has apologized for an affair with a woman the US believes was spying for China. The story could have profound implications for the world's most valuable company and the global AI race.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Amid protests, France's rising debt costs threaten stability</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3d16d78e606668e77de7aaa305e9997b11044c8611675b4c4c5b987a31d95e7</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654--50648477f294.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amid-protests-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France plans to spend an extra €4 billion on education amid nationwide protests. But with public debt mounting and interest costs climbing, how much fiscal room does the government have?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Tesla to 'wind down' production of flop Cybertruck</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5f9886da661835333f14336ebfe61bb395f3c43353629d665233d89ed458cc2</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tesla-to-wind-down-production-of-flop-cybertruck/a-79877759--ecdd4924ebad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tesla-to-wind-down-production-of-flop-cybertruck/a-79877759?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk's electric pickup for the future will start to be consigned to the past next year. The Cybertruck's bulk and crude shape meant it could only pass regulatory standards in more permissive markets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>European shares join a global sell-off as AI spending fears rattle Wall Street and Asian markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9d16cb166b3df7ec60d46146f33c8c4cc0efff1d8cb32227453fd394774c18b</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-shares-join-a-global-sell-off-as-ai-spending-fears-rattle-wall-street-and-asian-markets/a-79871504--c1f154c43d0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-shares-join-a-global-sell-off-as-ai-spending-fears-rattle-wall-street-and-asian-markets/a-79871504?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European shares have fallen after sharp losses in Asia and on Wall Street. Doubts over huge AI investments and fears of curbs following the Democrats' US midterm victory have rattled global markets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What the Democrats' midterms win means for the US economy and Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:598dc558cb0b30dd32790fe6901777c71772913c5f66a0863a93455f78f37f92</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T07:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716--124f824b0e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From high oil prices and data centers to tariffs and mounting debt, economic concerns played a key role in the crushing defeat of President Donald Trump's Republicans. So can the Democrats now make a difference?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>BMW reports lower Q3 earnings as China woes mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b134b8e7f7b2f5159bfa1349780b7f95f10d0dd2bc253fbf11600ca6679964e</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847--9f74c40c2952.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">BMW reports a drop in profits in the July to September quarter amid fierce competition from China.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Could AI give NFTs a second chance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d63d04a8d2b7ae6828558fe324fd2d000ac01fc1ba64d2bebba7d21622001ab</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T09:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-ai-give-nfts-a-second-chance/a-79840593--1d40731d5054.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-ai-give-nfts-a-second-chance/a-79840593?maca=en-rss-en-bus-2091-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">NFTs have plunged in value since their pandemic height in 2021. In some cases, they are worth 99% less than they were paid for. Yet tokenization of real-world assets and AI means the curios may yet have a future.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry></feed>
